  "independence": [
    "A separate Python oracle reads original CGFX signed-relative pointers, metadata words and interleaved vertex bytes directly. It does not call the C parser to determine expected values.",
    "Expected UVs are float32 pairs at stream offset24. Expected colors use byte components at offset32 multiplied by the stored float32 scale; the fixed-color shape reads its float4 directly, ignoring the fixed-buffer scale as SPICA Gfx.cs does.",
    "The C implementation is compiled to an isolated shared library and loaded through ctypes structures matching cgfx_model.h. Owned arrays are compared byte-for-byte; all exposed material fields and draw fields are compared to the independent oracle. Freeing is verified to zero the scene.",
    "The synthetic runtime fixture is separately authored in Python and embeds asymmetric Morton-tiled RGBA8 pixels, direct material command packets, interleaved UV/color attributes and explicit relative pointers. It does not copy original assets or the C unit fixture."
  ],
